`io_lib:format/2` returns an iolist; `io:format/2` writes. Erlang splits the
two modules for exactly that reason, and the row's own note conceded it —
"Returns iolist, not direct I/O, but typically written immediately" — while
AUTO_SINK_ZONE_MAP turned `logging` into an auto-derived taint SINK at every
call site. A boundary tag asserts the crossing happens AT THIS CALL, in this
call's scope (ADR-0049 ruling 1); "typically written immediately" describes a
different call, one hop later.

Removed against a finding-level proof, per ADR-0049 ruling 3, run per language
rather than argued. rabbitmq, both arms cold on separate XDG_CACHE_HOME with
the "No cached results found" line asserted rather than assumed — the survey
cache keys on repo CONTENT, so a shared cache would have handed arm B arm A's
answer and produced a clean fake null:

    host-secret-no-logging   violated in BOTH arms, 100 -> 68 flows
    sink modules             io_lib 94 -> 0,  io 5 -> 64
    rabbitmq#0/#4/#6         all three adjudicated TPs RE-ROOT onto io:format
    control                  the other six claims: evidence sets identical

CORRECTS MEASUREMENT 0006. Its sensitivity S1 projected useful precision at
21.4% on the assumption those three TPs would vanish. They do not, so nothing
is deducted and useful precision is unchanged at 24.1%. 0006 names the same
shape for urllib.request.Request two paragraphs later and calls it "an
attribution defect, not a vacuous claim" — it filed two identical shapes into
different buckets because the rule was never stated. Stated now: a row that
misattributes WHERE a crossing happens is an attribution defect; only a row
asserting a crossing that does not happen at all is vacuous.

The gate is DERIVED, which is the durable part. Pinning io_lib would catch
io_lib and nothing else. A general sweep for self-refuting notes returned 13
hits of which 11 were notes narrating a past removal — an 11-row exemption
list is a gate nobody maintains. Matching the rationalisation instead returns
exactly the live families in three languages, and found javascript's seven
`path.*` rows under fs_read on "not I/O but commonly precede fs_read" —
pinned as known-wrong-and-unfixed, not adjudicated-correct, because ruling 3's
proof runs per language and path.* has no obvious executor to re-root onto.

A wider hole underneath is filed, not papered over: some vanished flows were
REAL, logging via ?LOG_DEBUG, an OTP macro the analyzer never expands.
rabbitmq has 1,910 ?LOG_* uses against 187 direct `logger:` calls, so 91% of
its logging surface is invisible and io_lib was covering it by coincidence.

Filed: INV-zihor (the macro gap, P1), WI-tunod (javascript path.*),
